# Jace, Telepath Unbound's -3: "You may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard this turn. If that spell
# would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead." Not flashback (the rulings): the replacement is of the move to the
# graveyard alone (CR 614.1a), so a spell cast this way that leaves the stack for anywhere else goes there. Turn 1 Bot1
# sacrifices Black Lotus for three Lightning Bolts; Jace loots on turn 5, flips with five cards in the graveyard, and his -3
# lets a Bolt be cast from there at Bot2. Bot2's Remand returns it to Bot1's hand - not to exile, as Snapcaster Mage's
# flashback would - and Bot2 draws a card. Bot2 took the first three Bolts only: 20 - 9.

